<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Head setups</h4>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide in Table <a href="#S6.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 6.2 Head setups ‣ 6 Model Parameters ‣ Curia: A Multi-Modal Foundation Model for Radiology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> the different configurations used for each downstream tasks (see Fig.  <a href="#S4.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 4.2.1 Adapting the model for downstream tasks ‣ 4.2 Evaluation setting ‣ 4 Methods ‣ Curia: A Multi-Modal Foundation Model for Radiology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S6.T2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Head setup for all tasks for Curia models.<span id="S6.T2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report whether features were aggregated at the image level or within segmentation masks (see Fig. <a href="#S4.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ 4.2.1 Adapting the model for downstream tasks ‣ 4.2 Evaluation setting ‣ 4 Methods ‣ Curia: A Multi-Modal Foundation Model for Radiology" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). Additionally, we specify whether CLS tokens or patch tokens were used.</span></span></figcaption>
